  "voting_summary": "Utah is a vote-by-mail state: every active voter is mailed a ballot and nearly all vote by mail or drop box, though in-person voting sites are available, and results publish as combined totals only. Ballots postmarked the day before election day are accepted for up to two weeks. Polls close at 10 p.m. Eastern; a large pre-processed dump lands shortly after closing, followed by county batches over the following two weeks. Late batches have historically leaned slightly Democratic, tightening margins modestly during the canvass.",
